.TH IMUD\-MQTT 8 "2026-08-28" "imud 1.9.0" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-mqtt \- bridge imud's binary stream to MQTT with Home Assistant
discovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imud-mqtt
\&[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\&[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud-mqtt
connects to the local AF_UNIX binary subscription stream published by
.BR imud (8)
and publishes imud's attitude/heading/motion values to an MQTT broker as scalar
"one value per topic" messages, plus Home Assistant MQTT-discovery configs so
the sensors self-register as a single
.I imud
device.  imud's NMEA and Signal K outputs are unaffected.
.PP
The bridge holds no hardware.  It reads the stream socket named by its own
.B socket
key (default
.IR /run/imud/imud-stream.sock ),
so
.BR imud (8)
must have its
.B [stream]
output enabled.  libmosquitto's background loop owns the broker connection
(auto-reconnect and keepalive), so a broker outage never stalls the reader.
.PP
Values are published in human-friendly units by default
.RB ( units " = " deg :
degrees, ??/min, metres, ??C) or SI
.RB ( units " = " rad :
radians, rad/s).  Topics (default prefix
.IR imud ):
.PP
.RS 4
.TS
l l.
imud/navigation/headingMagnetic	always
imud/navigation/headingTrue	when declination is known
imud/navigation/magneticVariation	when declination is known
imud/navigation/rateOfTurn	always
imud/attitude/roll , /pitch , /yaw	always (imud NED convention)
imud/environment/heave	publish_heave, once heave settles
imud/environment/heaveRate	publish_heave, once heave settles (m/s)
imud/environment/waveHeight	publish_heave, once sea state settles (m, Hs)
imud/environment/wavePeriod	publish_heave, once sea state settles (s)
imud/environment/rollPeriod	publish_heave, once sea state settles (s)
imud/environment/rollAmplitude	publish_heave, once sea state settles (angle)
imud/environment/pitchPeriod	publish_heave, once sea state settles (s)
imud/environment/pitchAmplitude	publish_heave, once sea state settles (angle)
imud/imu/temperature	always
imud/engine/running	always; ON/OFF binary_sensor (engine detector)
imud/status/online	retained; \(dqoffline\(dq via MQTT last-will
.TE
.RE
.PP
Home Assistant discovery configs are published (retained) to
.IR <ha_prefix>/sensor/<client_id>_<sensor>/config .
The
.B heave
and
.B heaveRate
topics are withheld until the heave estimator has settled (~10\(mu\(*t), and
the sea-state topics
.RB ( waveHeight ", " wavePeriod ", " rollPeriod ", " rollAmplitude ", " pitchPeriod ", " pitchAmplitude )
until the wave statistics settle on top of that, so subscribers never see the
startup transient; their discovery configs are still advertised whenever
.B publish_heave
is set, so the Home Assistant entity exists and simply reads
.I unavailable
until then.
Raw high-rate accelerometer/gyro/magnetometer/quaternion data and the
gyro-bias / variance / quiescence diagnostics are intentionally not published
over MQTT (wrong transport / not Home-Assistant-relevant) \(em consume the
binary stream or the InfluxDB bridge for those.
.IP
MQTT bridge: reads imud's stream socket and publishes scalar
telemetry topics (+ Home Assistant discovery) to an MQTT broker.
Configured by [imud\-mqtt] in its own file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR PATH
Config file (default: \fI\,/etc/imud/imud\-mqtt.conf\/\fP)
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and exit
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print this help and exit
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration.  The publish rate, QoS, retain flag, units, heave
publishing, and log level are applied live; broker/client/topic-prefix changes
require a restart.  If the reload fails to parse, the running configuration is
kept.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Graceful shutdown (publishes a retained \(dqoffline\(dq availability message).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Read from
.I /etc/imud/imud-mqtt.conf
(the
.B [imud-mqtt]
section); the keys are documented in
.BR imud-mqtt.conf (5).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-mqtt.conf
Default configuration file, installed mode 0640 owner
.I root:imud
because it can hold a plaintext broker password.
A file that exists but cannot be read is fatal \(em the bridge refuses to start
rather than run on defaults.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run in the foreground against a local broker and watch the topics:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-mqtt --config /etc/imud/imud-mqtt.conf
mosquitto_sub -t 'imud/#' -v
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable as a service (after enabling imud's
.B [stream]
output and
.B broker_enabled
in
.IR imud-mqtt.conf ;
the daemon itself is enabled by default):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl enable --now imud-mqtt
.EE
.RE
